# nr-office-comrs-session-lifecycle: the session lifecycle of mixdog-office-com (src/office.rs, src/state/{mod,open,create,isolation,cleanup,chart_excel}.rs),
# tests/{cleanup,session,session_live}.rs and recorder/scenarios/session.json.
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave); the sources were checked to parse with rustfmt only.

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs (not a hot file, not owned by this task)
Module list: after `pub mod identity;` add `pub mod office;`, and after `mod session;` add `pub mod state;`:

    pub mod identity;
    pub mod office;
    pub mod platform;
    pub mod ps;
    pub mod host;
    mod oneshot;
    mod route;
    mod scripts;
    mod session;
    pub mod state;

and in the crate doc list nothing else changes (the modules carry their own docs).

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/platform/mod.rs (not owned by this task)
`Path.GetFullPath` for the session's paths is the platform layer's `full_path`; make it callable from the crate:

    -fn full_path(value: &str) -> Option<String> {
    +pub(crate) fn full_path(value: &str) -> Option<String> {

(src/office.rs `use crate::platform::full_path;`.)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets (autotests = false), after `[[test]] name = "host_protocol"`:

    [[test]]
    name = "cleanup"
    path = "tests/cleanup.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "session"
    path = "tests/session.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "session_live"
    path = "tests/session_live.rs"

No new dependency: the crate already depends on mixdog-fsio (Test-Path and CreateDirectory of a created document's folder, and the tests' scratch
directories through `Unlaned`), windows (IUnknown to IDispatch for the running object table's answer) and serde_json. No Cargo.lock or workspace-hack change.

## 4. What the actions task (nr-office-comrs-actions) builds on
The SessionHandler it registers in host/handlers.rs `registered()` keeps one `mixdog_office_com::state::SessionState` and calls:
  - `state::open_session_state(proof, &env, out, payload) -> Result<SessionState, String>` for `open_session` (it writes the early identity line itself and,
    on failure, the cleanup of what it built and the "; cleanup incomplete: ..." text), then `state::open_session_response(&mut state, &env)`;
  - `SessionState::record_foreground(platform)` for `record_foreground`;
  - `state::close_session(&mut state, &env, payload) -> Result<Closed, String>` for `close` (save, answer, cleanup; `Closed::closed` says the state is gone);
  - `state::close_session_state(&mut state, false, &env)` then `Emitter::cleanup_failure(&cleanup.to_value())` for `end`;
  - `state::session_response(&mut state, &env, &fields)` for every action's answer (isolation report first, the action's fields after).
`office::Env { platform, applications }` is what they all take: `platform` is the host's `WindowsPlatform`, `applications` is `office::LiveApplications`
(Windows) or, in tests, `office::ScriptedApplications` (feature test-support). `office::{prog_id_for_format, save_format_for_path, collection_for,
find_open_document, active_application, new_hidden_application, open_background_document, save_document, close_office_document, office_document_count,
initialize_owned_application, set_office_visible, item_of, text_of, long_of, same_document_path, get_full_path}` are the helpers of office-com-host.ps1 lines 11-121,
Save-Document and office-com-cleanup.ps1. `state::ChartExcel` (a field of `SessionState`, `pub chart_excel`) is the registry the chart-data slide operations
(nr-office-comrs-ppt-edit, `Register-PowerPointChartExcelApplication`) fill with `contains_application`, `insert_application(key, app)`, `add_process(pid)`;
`close_state` and the isolation read it. A one-shot host that needs the same registry owns a `ChartExcel` and calls `close(quit, &env)`.

## 5. Not in this task, stated so nobody looks for it
- tests/fixtures/session/ holds no recorded fixture: recording needs Windows PowerShell 5.1 and Microsoft Office on the migration PC
  (`node recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area session --dll <mixdog_office_com_recorder.dll>`), and tests/session.rs replays hand-written call logs until then.
- No protocol row, no SERVICE_PENDING change, no desktop change.
